  "notes": "よそう is a verb specifically for scooping and serving rice or soup from a larger container into individual bowls. It is typically written in kana.\n\nWRITING:\n- Sometimes written as {装|よそ}う, but kana is standard\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ご{飯|はん}をよそう: to serve rice\n- {味噌汁|みそしる}をよそう: to serve miso soup\n- {茶碗|ちゃわん}によそう: to serve into a bowl\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {盛|も}る: to heap, to pile food on a plate — used more broadly for plating food, not just scooping into bowls\n- よそう is specific to scooping from a pot/cooker into a bowl",
